{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Test Coverage Maintainer",
  "description": "Monitors file changes across frontend and backend, identifies missing test coverage, generates test cases for new/modified code, and runs relevant test suites to ensure quality",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "secure-gate-access/client/src/**/*.js",
      "secure-gate-access/client/src/**/*.jsx",
      "secure-gate-access/server/src/**/*.js",
      "secure-gate-access/server/**/*.js"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A source file has been modified. Please analyze the changes and ensure proper test coverage:\n\n1. **File Analysis**: Examine the modified file to identify:\n   - New or modified functions/methods\n   - New or updated React components (if frontend)\n   - New or modified API endpoints/routes (if backend)\n   - Changed business logic or data flows\n\n2. **Test Coverage Assessment**: \n   - Check if corresponding test files exist\n   - Verify if existing tests cover the modified functionality\n   - Identify gaps in test coverage for the changes\n\n3. **Test Generation** (if coverage is missing):\n   \n   **For Frontend Files** (client/src/**):\n   - Generate React Testing Library component tests for UI components\n   - Create Jest unit tests for utility functions and hooks\n   - Add integration tests for complex user flows\n   - Include accessibility tests where appropriate\n   \n   **For Backend Files** (server/src/**):\n   - Generate Jest unit tests for service functions\n   - Create Supertest integration tests for API endpoints\n   - Add database integration tests for data layer changes\n   - Include security and validation tests for new endpoints\n\n4. **Test Execution**:\n   - Run the relevant test subset to verify new/updated tests pass\n   - Check that existing tests still pass after the changes\n   - Report any test failures with suggested fixes\n\n5. **Coverage Analysis**:\n   - Calculate test coverage for the modified files\n   - Update coverage documentation if needed\n   - Flag critical modules that fall below coverage thresholds (80% for core business logic)\n   - Suggest additional test scenarios if coverage is insufficient\n\n6. **Quality Assurance**:\n   - Ensure tests follow project conventions and patterns\n   - Verify tests are maintainable and not brittle\n   - Check that tests cover both happy path and error scenarios\n   - Validate that tests properly mock external dependencies\n\nPlease provide a comprehensive analysis and generate any missing tests following the project's testing strategies and patterns outlined in the steering files."
  }
}